Here’s a solid `.gitignore` for a typical **Node.js + React** project:

```
# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Cache
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
.eslintcache

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE / Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# React Native (if applicable)
.expo/
.expo-shared/

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo
```

 Save it as **`.gitignore`** in your project's root directory.